answer:
According to [budget_2026_27_finance_bill.pdf, p.22-23], the following persons have income chargeable to tax under section 202 of the Income-tax Act:

(i) A domestic company whose income is chargeable to tax under section 200 or 201 of the said Act;
(ii) An individual or Hindu undivided family or association of persons, or body of individuals, whether incorporated or not, or an artificial juridical person referred to in section 2(77)(g) of the said Act whose income is chargeable to tax under section 202 of the said Act;
(iii) A co-operative society resident in India, whose income is chargeable to tax under section 203 or 204 of the said Act.

Additionally, according to [budget_2026_27_finance_bill.pdf, p.46-47], an assessee whose income is chargeable to tax under section 202 of the said Act.
